# Package

The unzipped folder must stay simple. The operator sees `atten.exe`. After the first run, `data` and `backups` appear beside it. Every DLL and locale folder lives in `app`.

## Version and names

Read `AppInfo.Version` and `Atten.App.csproj` `<Version>`. They must be the same string, for example `2.1`. Do not invent a different number for the zip or the tag.

| What | Name |
| --- | --- |
| Zip file | `atten-<version>-windows-x64.zip` |
| Folder inside the zip | `atten/` |
| Root exe | `atten.exe` (the net48 launcher, a few KB) |
| Real app | `atten/app/Atten.App.exe` |
| Git tag | `v<version>` |
| GitHub release title | `Atten <version>` |
| GitHub asset | the same zip file name |

Examples for `2.1`: `atten-2.1-windows-x64.zip`, tag `v2.1`, title `Atten 2.1`.

Lowercase `atten`, hyphen before the version, no `v` in the zip name, no spaces, always `windows-x64`.

Write the zip to `dist/` (gitignored). Do not commit `dist/`, `*.zip`, `bin/`, or `obj/`.

## How to build

Never zip a `bin/.../Release` **build** tree. That copies `win-x64/` again and adds `runtimes/win-arm64`.

```powershell
dotnet publish src/Atten.App/Atten.App.csproj -c Release -r win-x64 -p:Platform=x64 --self-contained true
dotnet build src/Atten.Launcher/Atten.Launcher.csproj -c Release
```

Publish folder: `src/Atten.App/bin/x64/Release/net8.0-windows10.0.19041.0/win-x64/publish/`

1. Copy the publish folder into `atten/app/`.
2. Copy `src/Atten.Launcher/bin/Release/net48/atten.exe` to `atten/atten.exe`.
3. Delete `*.pdb` and `createdump.exe` from `atten/app/`.
4. Zip the `atten` folder (so the archive root is `atten/`, not loose files).

Do not publish the launcher as self-contained. Do not put `Atten.App.exe` at the zip root.

## Must not be in the zip

- `runtimes/`, a nested `win-x64/`, `win-arm64`, `win-x86`
- `*.pdb`, `createdump.exe`
- `data/`, `backups/`, `atten.db`, WAL files
- A second copy of `atten.exe` inside `app/`
- Source, tests, `.cursor`, or the repo `data/` folder

## Check before you call it done

List the archive (`tar -tf` the zip) and confirm all of these:

- Top level is only `atten/atten.exe` and `atten/app/`
- `atten/app/Atten.App.exe` exists
- No `runtimes/`, no nested `win-x64/`, no `.pdb`, no `createdump`, no `data/`
- `atten.exe` at the root is about 10 KB, not tens of megabytes
- Zip size is about the same as the last release (~90 MB). Near 180 MB means extra architectures slipped in

`data` and `backups` are created at runtime beside `atten.exe`. `AppPaths` treats an exe inside `app` as published at the parent folder. Automatic snapshots sit beside `data`, not inside it.
